<concept id="t00379">
	<title>Shark fin antenna</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>infotainment system 
					<indexterm>antenna</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
				<indexterm>antenna</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e02683">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e02684">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV035024.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e02685"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>Shark-fin antenna transmit and receive signals such as AM/FM and <i>GPS</i>. Additional signals are sent and received according to vehicle options.</p>
		<note type="note">
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p>Be careful of antenna damage by checking the height of the vehicle before entering low-ceiling spaces such as automated parking lots or automated washing machines.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Be careful not to contact the antenna when loading cargo on the roof rack. Antenna transmission/reception performance may be degraded.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</note>
	</conbody>
</concept>